INT. STALLED FERRIS WHEEL GONDOLA - NIGHT

Dead carnival below. Fog. The gondola sways.

AUGUSTA "GUS" FELLOWES, 60s, retired carny, grips the rail. Across from him, TAMSIN OYELARAN, 20s, scrolls a dead phone. Beside her, a MAN IN A YELLOW RAINCOAT, face hidden under a hood, sits perfectly still.

GUS
(to both)
Operator'll be back. They always come back.

TAMSIN
(to Gus)
Who's they?

GUS
(muttering)
Nobody. Nobody's there.

Something below laughs. Tinny. Calliope music starts, off-key.

TAMSIN
Do you hear that?

The Man in the Yellow Raincoat lifts his head.

MAN IN YELLOW RAINCOAT
Ticket, please.

Gus pats his pockets. Tamsin shakes her head.

TAMSIN
We didn't buy tickets.

MAN IN YELLOW RAINCOAT
Everyone buys one.

The hood falls back. Painted grin. No eyes. Gus grabs Tamsin's wrist.

GUS
(low, to himself)
Pike. It's Pike. Not again.

PIKE
You remember me, Gus.

The gondola drops a foot. Stops. The grin widens.
